  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decreasing the burden of tuberculosis disease and halting the spread of drug resistance in eleven EECA countries through increasing political commitment and translating evidence into implementation of patient-centered TB models of care - World - Multicountry EECA PAS (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry EECA PAS, Tuberculosis, Center for Health Policies and Studies (PAS Center)This program has the following goals: To improve TB and drug resistant TB (DR-TB) outcomes in the targeted Eastern Europe and Central Asia (EECA) countries through a health system strengthening approach that leads to the wide adoption of patient centered approaches for the provision of TB and DR-TB prevention, treatment and care services.. The objectives of this program are: To develop and disseminate evidence on effective TB service delivery systems for implementation of patient-centered approaches and innovative models of care..  To ensure sustainable financing of TB control and efficient funds allocation mechanisms..  To increase political commitment to TB and M/XDRTB control through regional cooperation and evidence sharing for better governance of national TB programs.</narrative>
  </description>
